From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:36:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): hide teammate deliveries Claude records
 without an origin

Claude Code delivers an agent-team teammate's messages to the lead as
plain user records framed "Another Claude session sent a message:" plus
a <teammate-message> envelope and its own guidance paragraph, with no
origin field. The bridge only trusted origin.kind == "peer", so these
were persisted user_authored and rendered as raw markup and
idle_notification JSON in the lead's chat.

Typed and pasted prompts carry origin {"kind": "human"}, both as user
records and as prompts queued mid-turn, so treat a record or queued
prompt with no origin and Claude's complete framing (nothing else in
the text) as internal, like other peer traffic. Human-origin input and
framing with extra text still render as the user's message.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/claude-native-teammate-delivery; drop this copy once it
merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (fix: teammate deliveries no longer render as raw markup; no setting)
